      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new non-ionic water-soluble contrast medium was used for cervical myelography in 65 patients. The contrast medium was injected suboccipitally or by the latent C1-C2 approach. The films were of equally good quality as those obtained with other contrast media and tolerance has been superior. The contrast medium is Iopamidolo and is available in ampoules which is further positive quality."},
